# Licence

Three parts, three licences, because they are three different kinds of thing.
The full texts are in `LICENSES/`.

## The programs — MIT

`harness/`, and any script or tool in this repository, so far as they are this
project's to give. See `LICENSES/MIT.txt`. Take them, use them, sell what you
build with them.

Parts of the Voynich harness are not solely this project's, and those parts
carry their authors' terms as well as this one. See the section below.

## The data — CC BY 4.0

The saved runs in `work/rohonc/`, `harness/proposals.json`, the reader's
edition, the alignments, and the mechanical outputs generally.
See `LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt`. Build on them; credit this work.

## The translation and the editorial prose — CC BY-NC-ND 4.0

Book One and Book Two as published, the EPUB in `book/`, and the written
documents in this repository: `ROHONC.md`, `CONCLUSION.md`, `TESTS.md`,
`METHOD.md`, `RESULTS.md` and the rest.
See `LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0.txt`.

You may read it, quote it, teach from it, check it and republish it whole for
non-commercial purposes, with credit. You may not sell it, and you may not
publish an altered version of it. **The commercial rights to the English text
are reserved**, because a paperback of it is sold and the text is the thing
being sold.

Nothing here is meant to restrict examining the work. Quotation for review,
criticism, scholarship and reproduction of the results is what this is
published for, and the data and the programs, which are what you need in order
to check it, are under the permissive licences above.

## What is not this project's to license

**Other people's code inside `harness/`.** The Voynich harness ranks processes
that are somebody else's work, and most of them run from their own code: the
`text` and `struct` metric blocks are computed by calling Sachak's
`voynich-fingerprint` (MIT); Timm and Schinner's self-citation generator runs
from their own `text-generator.jar` (MIT); the grille and Llull generators
reimplement Antenore's `voynich-toolkit` (MIT); Greshko's Naibbe cipher
(`harness/generators/naibbe.py`, `naibbe_wb.py`) and Gaskell and Bowern's
gibberish samples (`harness/generators/gibberish.py`) are under **modified MIT
licences that require citation**, and that requirement travels with them. The
MIT grant above does not override any of it. `RESULTS.md` §9 is the complete
list, with each licence and what it supplied; the generator files mostly name
their source in their own first lines, but §9 is the authority, not the
file headers.

**The manuscript and the dictionary.** Levente Zoltán Király and Gábor Tokai's
dictionary, grammar and transcription are their published work. They are not
redistributed here and no licence over them is claimed or implied. The manuscript images belong to the Library of the
Hungarian Academy of Sciences. The manuscript itself is of the sixteenth
century and is out of copyright. `DATA_PROVENANCE.md` states the position on
every file.

Copyright 2026 Stephen Taylor.
